IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdcsa-types`

-- Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 — GOAL 1: THE MEASURES EVERY
-- ENTITLEMENT IS COUNTED IN (s 2; First Schedule).
--
--   "Which scheme does this child belong to; what is the eligibility date;
--    is this the parent's first, second or later specified event; what is
--    the weekly index; how long is '4 times the weekly index or 24 days'?"
--
-- Source: ../source/CDCSA2001.txt lines 109-327 (s 2), 4456-4555 (First Schedule).

§ `Goal 1 — the common measures`

§§ `Which scheme the child belongs to (s 2(1))`

-- s 2(1) "April 2025 Scheme child": "(a) a child born alive and whose mother's
-- confinement in respect of the child occurs on or after 1 April 2025, or
-- occurs before 1 April 2025 but the estimated delivery date for that
-- confinement is on or after that date; or (b) a child in respect of whom the
-- eligibility date of the application to adopt the child is on or after
-- 1 April 2025". "January 2024 Scheme child" is the same with 1 January 2024.
@ref s 2(1) "April 2025 Scheme child", "January 2024 Scheme child"
GIVEN start IS A DATE, e IS A `Child event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Scheme child from` start e IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a birth` b THEN
            NOT b's `stillborn`
        AND (   b's `confinement on` AT LEAST start
             OR b's `estimated delivery date` AT LEAST start)
    WHEN `an adoption` a THEN
        `the eligibility date of` a AT LEAST start

GIVEN e IS A `Child event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an April 2025 Scheme child` e IF `a Scheme child from` (YMD 2025 4 1) e

GIVEN e IS A `Child event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a January 2024 Scheme child` e IF `a Scheme child from` (YMD 2024 1 1) e

-- s 2(1) "eligibility date": "(a) if the child is a citizen or permanent
-- resident of Singapore, the date on which the application to adopt the child
-- is made; or (b) if the child is not ..., the date on which a dependant's pass
-- is issued in respect of the child". No pass issued yet: no eligibility date.
@ref s 2(1) "eligibility date"
GIVEN a IS AN Adoption
GIVETH A DATE
`the eligibility date of` a MEANS
    IF a's `the child is a citizen or permanent resident when the application is made`
    THEN a's `application made on`
    ELSE CONSIDER a's `dependant's pass issued on`
         WHEN JUST d  THEN d
         WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "no dependant's pass has been issued, so there is no eligibility date yet"

-- The date entitlements run from: the confinement, or the eligibility date.
GIVEN e IS A `Child event`
GIVETH A DATE
`the event date of` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a birth` b     THEN b's `confinement on`
    WHEN `an adoption` a THEN `the eligibility date of` a

-- The child's date of birth (an adoption's child; a birth's confinement).
GIVEN e IS A `Child event`
GIVETH A DATE
`the child's birth date in` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a birth` b     THEN b's `confinement on`
    WHEN `an adoption` a THEN a's `child born on`

§§ `First, second or later specified event (s 2(2))`

-- s 2(2): "(a) if the relevant specified event occurs before 1 November 2021,
-- any previous specified event of the woman is to be disregarded if, at the
-- time of the relevant specified event, either of the following applies to
-- each child from the previous specified event: (i) the child is dead or was a
-- stillborn child; (ii) the child has been adopted by another person (other
-- than jointly with the woman); (aa) if the relevant specified event occurs on
-- or after 1 November 2021, any previous specified event of the woman is to be
-- disregarded if ... each child from that previous specified event has been
-- adopted by another person (other than jointly with the woman); and (b) any
-- previous specified event involving an application by the woman to adopt a
-- child is to be disregarded if ... the application has been withdrawn or
-- refused."
@ref s 2(2)
GIVEN relevant IS A DATE, earlier IS A LIST OF `Earlier specified event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the specified event number on` relevant `, earlier events` earlier MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD NOT `disregarded` p) earlier) PLUS 1
    WHERE
        `disregarded` p MEANS
                p's `an adoption application since withdrawn or refused`
            OR  (IF relevant LESS THAN YMD 2021 11 1
                 THEN p's `each child is dead or was stillborn` OR p's `each child adopted by another person, not jointly with her`
                 ELSE p's `each child adopted by another person, not jointly with her`)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a first or second specified event` n IF n AT MOST 2

§§ `Age (s 2(2A))`

-- s 2(2A): a person attains an age "on the relevant anniversary"; a person born
-- on 29 February has the anniversary on 28 February in a common year.
-- `add years` moves 29 February to 28 February.
@ref s 2(2A)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, on IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age in years of a person born` born `, on` on MEANS
    `count from` 0
    WHERE
        `count from` n MEANS IF `add years` born (n PLUS 1) AT MOST on THEN `count from` (n PLUS 1) ELSE n

-- "below 12 months of age": before the first anniversary.
@ref ss 2(1) "specified event" (b)-(d); 12AC(1)(d)
GIVEN born IS A DATE, on IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `below 12 months of age, born` born `, on` on IF
    on LESS THAN `add years` born 1

§§ `The weekly index (First Schedule)`

-- Part 1: item 1 "Number of work days in a week"; item 2 "T/W"; item 3 "T/3",
-- the formulas the PDF prints as images (PROVENANCE.md). Note 3: a day of 5
-- hours or less counts as half a work day (the caller counts T so). Note 3A:
-- "the maximum number of work days is 6".
@ref First Schedule Part 1 items 1-3, notes 3, 3A
GIVEN p IS A `Work pattern`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly index for` p MEANS
    `at most 6` (CONSIDER p
                 WHEN `the same number of work days every week` d          THEN d
                 WHEN `a pattern repeated over a fixed number of weeks` t w THEN t DIVIDED BY w
                 WHEN `no regular pattern` t                               THEN t DIVIDED BY 3)
    WHERE
        `at most 6` x MEANS IF x GREATER THAN 6 THEN 6 ELSE x

-- Note 5: "Any duration calculated under this Act as a multiple of the weekly
-- index, if not a whole number of days, is to be rounded down to the nearest
-- half-day or whole day."
@ref First Schedule Part 1 note 5
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to the half day` x MEANS FLOOR (x TIMES 2) DIVIDED BY 2

-- "k times the employee's weekly index or 6k days, whichever is the lower" —
-- the Act's recurring week-equivalent (k = 1, 2, 4, 8, N).
@ref ss 9(1)(c)(ii), 9A(4), 10(2), 12AA(5), 12DB, 12F(2), 12H(1)(b), 12I(3); First Schedule note 5
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER, wi IS A NUMBER, `cap days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` k `times the weekly index` wi `or` `cap days` MEANS
    IF `multiple` LESS THAN `cap days` THEN `multiple` ELSE `cap days`
    WHERE
        `multiple` MEANS `rounded down to the half day` (k TIMES wi)

§§ `Capped payments`

-- The caps all read "an amount that does not exceed $X for every period
-- equal in duration to [a week-equivalent] ... and ... a total of $Y". For
-- `blocks` such periods paid at `pay per block`, the most payable.
@ref ss 9A(4)-(5), 10(2), 12AA(5), 12AB(2), 12AD(2), 12DB, 12F(2)-(3), 12G(2), 12I(3)-(4), 12J(2), 12JA(4)
GIVEN `cap per block` IS A NUMBER, `total cap` IS A NUMBER, blocks IS A NUMBER, `pay per block` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`at most` `cap per block` `per block and` `total cap` `in all, for` blocks `blocks paid at` `pay per block` MEANS
    IF `uncapped` GREATER THAN `total cap` THEN `total cap` ELSE `uncapped`
    WHERE
        `per block` MEANS IF `pay per block` GREATER THAN `cap per block` THEN `cap per block` ELSE `pay per block`
        `uncapped`  MEANS blocks TIMES `per block`
